{"book":11,"chapter":12,"rubric":"MODERN FRONTEND / THE JAVASCRIPT LANGUAGE / CHAPTER 12","slides":[{"title":"FP ecosystem","sub":"Chapter 12 · What grew out of the ideas","short":"Introduction","main":"Libraries solve different problems: utilities, immutability, types, streams.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Utilities","Immutable data","Streams and types"],"captions":["JavaScript has many libraries for functional style, each with different goals","Some offer a set of utilities, others immutable updates","Others give sum types and event streams; we look at the ideas and write small versions"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"l0","x":100.0,"y":70.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"lodash/fp","tone":"yellow","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"l1","x":260.0,"y":70.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Ramda","tone":"yellow","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"l0","x":100.0,"y":70.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Immer","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"l1","x":260.0,"y":70.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Immutable.js","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"l0","x":100.0,"y":70.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"fp-ts · Effect","tone":"blue","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"l1","x":260.0,"y":70.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"RxJS","tone":"blue","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[10.7,28.7]}]},{"title":"lodash and lodash/fp","sub":"Utilities and the fp variant","short":"lodash","main":"In the fp variant functions are curried and data goes last.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["lodash","lodash/fp","Fixed arity"],"captions":["lodash is a set of utilities: grouping, path access, multi-key sorting, debounce; much is already in the language","lodash/fp reshapes them into functional style: curried, non-mutating, data as the last parameter","Fixed arity: map passes no extra arguments, so the famous parseInt trap disappears"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":44.0,"lines":["import { groupBy, get } from 'lodash-es';","","groupBy(users, 'city');"],"hl":[2],"lang":"js","size":10.5,"lh":24.0,"w":310.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["import fp from 'lodash/fp';","","const names = fp.pipe(","  fp.filter('active'),","  fp.map('name'),",")(users);"],"hl":[3,4],"lang":"js","size":10.0,"lh":20.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":44.0,"lines":["['1','2','3'].map(parseInt)      // [1, NaN, NaN]","fp.map(parseInt)(['1','2','3'])  // [1, 2, 3]"],"hl":[0],"bad":[0],"lang":"js","size":9.0,"lh":30.0,"w":320.0}]],"cues":[16.9,29.9]}]},{"title":"Ramda","sub":"Everything curried","short":"Ramda","main":"Uniformity and argument order are Ramda's strength; readability is the trap.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Everything curried","assoc, path, evolve","Placeholder"],"captions":["Ramda is functional from the first line: all functions curried, data last, nothing mutated","assoc and assocPath return a copy with a new field, path reads a value, evolve transforms fields","R.__ skips an argument in partial application; point-free chains are both a strength and a readability trap"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["const total = R.pipe(","  R.filter(R.propEq('paid', 'status')),","  R.map(R.prop('sum')),","  R.sum,",")(orders);"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"js","size":9.5,"lh":20.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["R.assoc('age', 37, user)","R.assocPath(['a', 'b'], 1, obj)","R.path(['a', 'b', 0], obj)","R.evolve({ age: R.inc }, user)"],"lang":"js","size":10.0,"lh":22.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":44.0,"lines":["const minus10 = R.subtract(R.__, 10);","minus10(25)   // 15"],"hl":[0],"lang":"js","size":11.0,"lh":28.0,"w":320.0}]],"cues":[10.4,31.1]}]},{"title":"Immer","sub":"produce and the draft","short":"Immer","main":"Change the draft, get an immutable result.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["produce","Proxy draft","Patches"],"captions":["produce(state, draft => …): you change the draft the usual way: assign fields, call push","The draft is a proxy: it records changes, then a new state is built; only touched nodes are copied","If nothing changed, the same reference comes back; patches are a list of changes to send or undo"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["const next = produce(state, (d) => {","  d.user.age++;","  d.items.push(item);","});"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"js","size":10.5,"lh":22.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"s","x":90.0,"y":50.0,"w":80.0,"h":26.0,"text":"state","tone":"blue","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"d","x":90.0,"y":100.0,"w":80.0,"h":26.0,"text":"draft (Proxy)","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n","x":270.0,"y":76.0,"w":80.0,"h":26.0,"text":"next","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":90.0,"y1":64.0,"x2":90.0,"y2":88.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":130.0,"y1":100.0,"x2":230.0,"y2":82.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["produce(state, () => {}) === state   // true","","const [next, patches, inverse] =","  produceWithPatches(state, recipe);"],"hl":[0,3],"lang":"js","size":9.5,"lh":22.0,"w":330.0}]],"cues":[17.7,33.1]}]},{"title":"Persistent structures","sub":"Shared parts of versions","short":"Persistent","main":"Only the path to the changed cell is copied.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Shared parts","Path to the cell","Immutable.js"],"captions":["Persistent structures share unchanged parts between versions: a new version does not copy everything","Only the path from the root to the changed cell is copied: appending to a wide tree is almost constant time","Immutable.js offers such structures with its own API; plain objects and Immer are more common"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":100.0,"y":60.0,"w":70.0,"h":26.0,"text":"v1","tone":"blue","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":250.0,"y":60.0,"w":70.0,"h":26.0,"text":"v2","tone":"green","